description: Lean context and cost habits — avoid bulk-loading rules and agents
alwaysApply: true
---

# Context budget

- **Short chats** - one task per chat; do not drag long threads.
- **Narrow tools** - no `@` whole dirs, no monorepo/log/CI dumps.
- **Ask for Q&A** - `/ask` or Ask mode; Agent only when editing.
- **One agent** - no spare subagents; no parallel explore+implement+review unless asked.
- Do **not** bulk-read `.config/rules/`, `.cursor/rules/`, agents, or skills “just in case”.
- Trust glob-applied rules. Open a rule/skill only when in scope or invoked.
- Commits / PRs / landing design live in project rules - not duplicated User Rules.
